### Core Tactical Engine Breakdown

1. **Heavy Physical Direction Locks ($D$-Stance $\sim 50\text{--}52\%$):**
Against higher difficulty search tiers (`master` and `soul`), Nigo's policy relies primarily on `D+L` (*Punches*, 140 base damage) and `D+I` (*Mixed Combo*, 130 base damage). Chaining identical directional commands avoids the 1% charge reset penalty, maintaining high execution speed while yielding continuous +2 Chi per hit.
2. **Special Priority Overrides ($S$-Stance $\sim 40\text{--}48\%$):**
Nigo leverages $S$-stance priority (`S+L` *Rider Power Kick*, 860 base; `S+J` *Rider Punch*, 370 base) to interrupt X's wind-ups (`D+L` *Ridol Rod Strike* and `D+I` *Ridol Whip Lash*).
3. **Exceptionally Low Faint Exposure ($2.4\%\text{--}4.3\%$ IDLE):**
Nigo maintains exceptionally low forced recovery rates (`DO_NOTHING @ 0%`), averaging under 4% across all matches. By controlling engagement timing, Nigo avoids X's high-damage `S+I` (*Vacuum Hell Wheel*, 1111 base) and forces X into 100 Faint locks instead.

